+/// Whether [dylib] takes an environment as the first model-loading argument.
+/// `LiteRtCreateModelFromFd` is absent from the 2.1.5 dylib and present in the
+/// newer runtimes (LiteRT-LM's libLiteRt.so on Linux), so on desktop its
+/// presence identifies the newer ABI. Not on iOS: the runtime this plugin
+/// loads there (`litert-ios-v1.0.1`) exports it, yet its model loaders take
+/// no environment (`LiteRtCreateModelFromBuffer(buffer, size, model)`), and
+/// passing one first fails every model with
+/// kLiteRtStatusErrorInvalidFlatbuffer.
+bool _hasEnvironmentModelAbi(DynamicLibrary dylib) =>
+    Platform.isAndroid ||
+    (!Platform.isIOS && dylib.providesSymbol('LiteRtCreateModelFromFd'));
 
